{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/915121-renown-who-what-can-award-it","id":915121,"title":"Renown - Who/What Can Award It","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T15:15:12-07:00","id":915121,"title":"Renown - Who/What Can Award It","content":"Hail friends.<br /> <br /> This is something I've been pondering - the Anshega totems can give Renown, and so can the Lunes...but what about those Uratha who are Ghost Wolf and unaligned with/hate Luna? For such an all-important stat, you're kind of stuck taking it from either Anshega totems or Lunes. Any idea for alternative sources?<br /> <br /> I generally rule that a spirit of Rank 7 or above would have the ability to grant Renown, but the question, of course, is making the extremely complex and epic pact involved in creating another Renown sponsor. Helios, theoretically, fulfills this role, although his personality (unchangingly surly) makes him an extremely unlikely candidate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:20:03-07:00","id":915170,"title":"","content":"Simply Strengthen allows a spirit with the relevant influence (Cunning, Glory, Honor, Purity, Wisdom).<br /> <br /> Spirits tasked (read: with bans) regarding the awarding of renown wouldn't give two shits about an Uratha's personal opinion of their spiritual forebear when the subject does something deserving or recognition. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:47:52-07:00","id":915182,"title":"","content":"Wait wait wait. So if a spirit has a single dot in one of the relevant influences, it can award renown? What about Lunes who don't have dots in the relevant influence who still reward Renown? I wouldn't want to bother Forsaken players with visiting every Lune with the right influence. Besides, Renown seems like some *serious* Juju, since it contributes directly to a Werewolf's sheer might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:48:55-07:00","id":915183,"title":"","content":"Providing you're not a Pure, you'll always likely be given renown by lunes. They serve the patron of the werewolves, who may be able to know everything werewolves do. And Luna is fickle and mercurial, she doesn't seem to particularly care if you're committing genocide or being a peacenik, providing you do worthy deeds.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, while it may have changed in second edition, the Pure tribal totems don't give them their renown. They give it to themselves through judgment by the pack and other respected Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:21:57-07:00","id":915204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/915121-renown-who-what-can-award-it?p=915182#post915182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Lunes who don't have dots in the relevant influence who still reward Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then their purpose, or duties doesn't includes the awarding of renown.<br /> <br /> A spirit can sense things that resonate with their influence literally from miles away. A spirit can literally look at your character, and in the influence was fear and cunning, it could literally tell your worst fears and when was the last time you were deserving of greater renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:41:37-07:00","id":915213,"title":"","content":"The pure give renown through ritual scarification, if I remember correctly. Part of what makes their brands blaze red in the shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:02:47-07:00","id":915573,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses y'all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}